Day 44: The Night Love Kneels | Holy Thursday (Mass of the Lord’s Supper)

📌 YouTube Description
Tonight we enter the Sacred Triduum —
the holiest days of the Christian year,
the hours where love bends low,
where God kneels before humanity,
where the heart of Jesus is revealed in humility, tenderness, and sacrifice.

Welcome to Day 44 of our Lent journey.
This is Holy Thursday — the night of the Upper Room, the night of the basin and the towel, the night of the Eucharist, the night love becomes visible. Jesus kneels before His disciples, washing the feet of those who will misunderstand Him, abandon Him, and deny Him. And still, He loves them. Completely.

This spoken‑word devotional invites you into the mystery of a love that holds nothing back — a love that serves, a love that pours itself out, a love that becomes the very food that sustains the world.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why Holy Thursday reveals the heart of Christ in humility and service

How Jesus gives Himself fully in the Eucharist and in the washing of feet

Why this night is not just a memory but a call to self‑giving love

A prayer to love as Jesus loves

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Jesus, let my love look like Yours.”

